From 909c9ab2f2a043714d3934ba1f01fde2b971f165 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:54:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Audio] The speakers a receiver declares: its EDID on
 any output, its room blocks, its ELD, kept up to date

With an AV receiver of 5.1.2 and Dolby Atmos passed through on a
GeForce, the Audio page of the player information said "Speakers: not
known yet; objects: if the receiver decodes them" for the whole film.

What a display or receiver declares was read from one place only: the
EDID of the display that Kodi shows on, and only where the audio engine
had said which output its sink opened and that output's ELD named that
display. "not known yet" came whenever that one entry was missing from
what the audio engine last said, and nothing replaced it: a listing of
the outputs again after a change of their count (an HDMI output whose
ELD comes after the sink opened, as NVIDIA's comes with the display)
that did not reopen the sink was never said at all, and a receiver on
an HDMI output of its own was never read ("the sound goes to another
display").

Now (SpeakerPlan.h, DeclaredBy()):
- the output is the one the sink opened or, while that is not said, the
  output of the path in use (passthrough or PCM);
- the EDID is that of its display on whichever output of the graphics
  cards has it: the display Kodi shows on, or another output of this
  card or of the others surveyed for the sound
  (CDRMUtils::EdidOfSoundDisplay());
- what it declares is its Speaker Allocation Data Block, its Room
  Configuration Data Block (CTA-861-G, the same three bytes) and the
  named places of its Speaker Location Data Block, as libdisplay-info
  0.4.0 reads them; heights included;
- where no output has that display, its ELD (which ALSA now keeps with
  each output): the first byte of the allocation and its formats, no
  heights, and the page says so ("ELD only: no heights");
- the audio engine says its outputs again after every listing of them
  (HandleDeviceCountChange()), and the page works it out again each time
  it is published, so an ELD that comes later or changes with a mode is
  taken at once; "not known yet" stays only while the output or its
  display is truly not known.
kodi.log says what is declared and from where each time that changes
("the speakers that the display or receiver declares: 5.1.2 by AVR-X3800H
(the EDID of the display shown)").
